  "query_preview": "..\nNumerous locally heavy showers and isolated to scattered\nthunderstorms continue to build tonight as the outer rainbands of \nBavi move in, and conditions will continue to deteriorate hereafter. \nGusty north winds of 15 to 25 mph will gradually increase across the \nislands tonight, then rapidly increase tomorrow afternoon as tropical\nstorm conditions, including sustained winds of 39 mph or more, begin\nto move into the coastal waters. Typhoon force winds of 74 mph or \ngreater are expected from early Monday morning to early Monday \nafternoon, with peak, potentially super typhoon conditions forecast \nto arrive late in the morning to around noon. The southern Marianas, \nincluding Guam and Rota, can generally expect winds to shift west to \nsouthwest during passage, while Tinian and Saipan may see north to \nnorth-northwest winds rapidly shift east, then south to southeast as\nthe storm passes. This narrow time range and wind shifts are highly \ndependent on Bavi's eventual arrival time and location of its \npassage, and uncertainty exists. After typhoon conditions pass, \nstrong southerly tropical storm winds (58 to 73 mph) will continue \nthrough the late afternoon to early evening Monday. Then, winds are \nexpected to fall below tropical storm conditions during the early \nmorning hours of Tuesday. See the Tropical Systems section below for \nmore details on Super Typhoon Bavi.",
